Verdict:
  The literal H=7 point alpha=(3,0) has zero masks and zero classes, as expected.
  E7 C5 metagraph holes are not the same object as the directed pentagon support:
  the directed C5 support maps to a single E7 vertex class, while a metagraph C5
  is a five-class quotient cycle.  The useful bridge is therefore not an exact
  identification of E7 C5 holes with Omega=K3.  It is an obstruction-layer
  analogy: both are first odd cycles created by cycle-space closure after scalar
  data forgets incidence.

Tournament Analysis:
  vertices = {E7_C5_hole_classes, directed_C5_support_class, near_h7_P3,
